-``--tone-mapping-metric=<standard|bt2020-itp|bt2020-adaptive|bt2020-rgb|maxrgb-itp|maxrgb-adaptive|maxrgb-rgb>``
+``--tone-mapping-metric=<standard|bt2020-rgb|maxrgb-rgb>``
     Selects the brightness metric for renderer-generated dynamic tone mapping.
     ``standard`` uses libplacebo's normal brightness metric.
-    The three ``bt2020`` modes use mpv-ht's smooth, homogeneous approximation of
-    the selected literal p=1 BT.2020 perceptual coordinate. ``bt2020-itp``
-    applies the metric-derived compression to I while retaining libplacebo's
-    normal conservative ITP chroma processing. ``bt2020-adaptive`` retains
-    progressively more source IPT chroma for saturated pixels while keeping
-    the same metric-derived I coordinate. ``bt2020-rgb`` applies the exact
+    ``bt2020-rgb`` uses mpv-ht's smooth, homogeneous approximation of the
+    selected literal p=1 BT.2020 perceptual coordinate. It applies the exact
     fixed-hue inverse along the linear RGB ray.
 
-    The three ``maxrgb`` modes use per-pixel ``max(R,G,B)`` for both the
+    ``maxrgb-rgb`` uses per-pixel ``max(R,G,B)`` for both the
     percentile/average frame statistics that generate the curve and the
-    per-pixel curve lookup. ``maxrgb-itp`` applies the resulting compression
-    to I with conservative chroma processing, ``maxrgb-adaptive`` uses the
-    same adaptive chroma retention, and ``maxrgb-rgb`` applies it exactly
-    along the linear RGB ray.
+    per-pixel curve lookup, applying it along the linear RGB ray.
+
+    The retired ``bt2020-itp``/``bt2020-adaptive`` and
+    ``maxrgb-itp``/``maxrgb-adaptive`` names are accepted as compatibility
+    aliases for the corresponding RGB-ray metric. Adaptive chroma is removed.
 
     These modes are used only for generic, pixel-measured DTM. If tone mapping is
     inactive, peak measurement is disabled or unavailable, HDR10+ authored
@@ -7800,14 +7797,6 @@ them.
     and retain the normal source-gain and peak limits. Has no effect when
     Contrast Shaping is inactive. (``--vo=gpu-next`` only)
 
-``--tone-mapping-adaptive-chroma-strength=<0..100>``
-    Controls how strongly the ``bt2020-adaptive`` and ``maxrgb-adaptive``
-    modes restore chroma removed by libplacebo's normal ITP hull processing.
-    ``0`` is identical to the corresponding ``itp`` mode, while ``100``
-    reproduces the full adaptive formula. The default is ``50``. This option
-    does not alter the selected brightness metric, peak measurements, temporal
-    smoothing, tone curve, or final gamut mapping. (``--vo=gpu-next`` only)
-
 ``--tone-mapping-ambient-gamma=<0.5..1.5>``
